## Corrected Interpretation

可寫入報告的說法：

> Mode B Round 2 evaluated `impl3_shape_dispatch_impl1_small_impl2_large`, a shape-aware dispatch candidate. The candidate dispatches slices 128 and 256 to the unchanged `impl=1` path and dispatches slices 784, 1024, and 2048 to the unchanged `impl=2` path validated in Round 1 for large slices. All five official slices passed correctness in three trials. The small slices should be interpreted as measurement-equivalent baseline-preserving cases, not as kernel optimizations. The large slices retained valid per-slice improvements of approximately 1.297x, 1.601x, and 1.325x against the paired `impl=1` baseline, subject to CV verification from `results.csv`. Overall, Round 2 is best classified as a shape-aware dispatch / `PARAM_TUNE` result rather than a universal `KERNEL_OPT`.

